reproduce='''<div class="wrap"><section class="subhero"><span class="eyebrow">Reproduction / software / interfaces</span><h1>Inspect, run,<br>then extend.</h1><p>Start with saved plans and software tests. Use the dated evidence directories to distinguish the original experiment from the corrected executor.</p></section><section class="section" id="stack"><h2>The software that actually runs.</h2><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Used in this project</th><th>Role / evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Host</td><td>Windows 11 + WSL Ubuntu 22.04</td><td>ROS and simulation run inside WSL.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Language planning</td><td>Python · gpt-4o-mini · temperature 0</td><td>One API call, JSON-object mode, named locations. <a href="../../src/planner.py">Planner source</a>.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Data contract</td><td>JSON Schema · jsonschema</td><td>Historical evaluation schemas remain unchanged. A separate September runtime contract gates execution.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Middleware</td><td>ROS2 Humble · Cyclone DDS</td><td>Loopback configuration for this WSL host. A distributed physical deployment needs a different network configuration.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Simulation</td><td>Gazebo Classic 11 · TurtleBot3 Waffle</td><td>Scripted warehouse, simulated range sensor and ground-truth odometry.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Global planning</td><td>NavFn · <code>use_astar: false</code></td><td><code>nav2_navfn_planner/NavfnPlanner</code> in the saved configuration.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Path following</td><td>Regulated Pure Pursuit</td><td>Desired linear speed 0.26 m/s; 0.25 m / 0.25 rad goal tolerances.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Costmaps</td><td>Static, obstacle / voxel, inflation layers</td><td>Configured scan observations on <code>/scan</code>; inflated obstacles guide navigation clearance.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Recovery</td><td>Nav2 behaviour server and per-step executor policies</td><td>Configured spin/back-up/wait behaviours; explicit abort, skip, retry, perimeter and later fallback handling.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Localisation in the recorded simulation</td><td>Map server + static map→odom transform</td><td>Ground truth. SLAM Toolbox was not used to obtain these runs.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Figures and documents</td><td>Matplotlib · LaTeX/IEEEtran · BibTeX</td><td>Data-driven figures with PNG, SVG and PDF exports; eight-page report draft.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div><p class="small">Source of implementation details: <a href="../../ros2_ws/src/nl_nav2_executor/params/nav2_params.yaml">Nav2 parameters</a>, <a href="../../ros2_ws/src/nl_nav2_executor/launch/warehouse_sim.launch.py">simulation launch</a>, <a href="../../setup/sim-env.sh">environment script</a>. Listed plugins are configured components; this is not a claim that every behaviour was triggered in the demos.</p></section>
<section class="section body-copy"><span class="eyebrow">01 / No API key required</span><h2>Run the software checks.</h2><pre><code># From the repository root, using an environment with pytest + jsonschema:
python -m pytest ros2_ws/src/nl_nav2_executor/test -q

# Deterministic replay of the saved v3 branch, with A unavailable:
python ros2_ws/src/nl_nav2_executor/scripts/dry_run.py \\
  --plan docs/validation/execution-check-20260911T172852Z/v3-L4-12-trial0.json \\
  --blocked storage_zone_a</code></pre><p>The expected successful visit is <code>storage_zone_b</code>. Without <code>--blocked</code>, only A is visited. Blocking both A and B produces exit code 1. These are mock navigation checks; no robot moves.</p><pre><code># WSL: rebuild and verify installed ROS imports and runtime resources
bash setup/verify-runtime-fixes.sh</code></pre></section>
<section class="section body-copy"><span class="eyebrow">02 / In WSL Ubuntu 22.04</span><h2>Run the actual warehouse.</h2><pre><code># ROS2 Humble, Gazebo Classic 11, Nav2 and TurtleBot3 packages must be installed.
source setup/sim-env.sh
cd ros2_ws
colcon build --packages-select nl_nav2_executor --symlink-install
source install/setup.bash
ros2 launch nl_nav2_executor warehouse_sim.launch.py</code></pre><p>In a second terminal, from the repository root:</p><pre><code>source setup/sim-env.sh
source ros2_ws/install/setup.bash
ros2 run nl_nav2_executor execute_plan \\
  --plan docs/validation/execution-check-20260911T172852Z/v2-L1-01-trial0.json \\
  --map map/warehouse_map.json</code></pre><p>Wait for both the map-server and navigation lifecycle managers to be active. The robot starts at the charging dock. Exit code 0 means completed execution; 1 means incomplete, aborted or deferred; 2 means rejected input. A fallback success is reported separately from reaching the primary destination.</p><div class="note">The current executor differs from the one used for the earlier 9/9 replays. See <a href="../validation/runtime-fixes-20260912/README.md">the correction record</a> and its preserved original files. Running old plans on new code is not an exact reproduction of old runtime behaviour.</div></section>
<section class="section body-copy"><span class="eyebrow">03 / Optional live model call</span><h2>Type a new command.</h2><pre><code># Configure an API key privately in the environment or local .env.
# The following command makes one billed API call.
export PROMPT_VERSION=v2
python src/run_pipeline.py "Go to the loading dock" \\
  --out /tmp/warehouse-plan.json</code></pre><p>The bridge validates the returned plan before writing an executable output. A clarification response does not trigger navigation. Select v3 explicitly for the fallback representation; the default planner prompt in the existing source remains v1 unless <code>PROMPT_VERSION</code> is set.</p></section>
<section class="section body-copy"><span class="eyebrow">04 / Visual artifacts</span><h2>Rebuild the presentation material.</h2><pre><code># In a Python environment with Matplotlib:
python setup/build-portfolio-figures.py
python setup/build-portfolio-pages.py

# Open docs/portfolio/index.html directly, or serve the repository locally:
python -m http.server 8765 --bind 127.0.0.1
# Then visit http://127.0.0.1:8765/docs/portfolio/

# Genuine new Gazebo captures (WSL; requires Xvfb, ImageMagick, xdotool):
bash setup/capture-portfolio.sh
bash setup/capture-portfolio.sh detail</code></pre><p>Capture scripts create dated directories and stop only the process groups they launch. Raw frame sequences and ROS logs stay out of the presentation pack. The report is rebuilt outside this repository while it is under assessment.</p><a href="MEDIA.md">Media export and attribution notes →</a></section></div>'''
(OUT/"reproduce.html").write_text(page("Reproduction and software",reproduce),encoding="utf-8")
